  Yes, but I use a technique I call "the inventory stare."  Just 
sit and stare at the inventory, bag of holding, and stash 
contents for tens of minutes at a time, with pauses for 
reflection.  


  I also do this every so often in non-abandoned games.  It's the
only real way I have of "getting the picture" of the game.  Don't
want to die when something in my inventory could have saved me.  
You don't need notes to do this, either.


  It also helps to have standard inventory letters for anything I
find handy.  And I break the game down into "sub-games" with 
definite, limited, sub-goals which are almost always done in the
same order.


  (It also helps to always play chaotic human wizards. ;-)



